Part 3: Self-Attention (Query, Key, Value)

This is the breakthrough introduced in the paper:

Attention Is All You Need

Everything in GPT, Gemini, Claude, DeepSeek, and Llama revolves around this idea.

The Problem

Suppose we have:

Prometheus collects metrics.
It stores them.

Question:

Who is "It"?

Humans immediately know:

It → Prometheus

How can a machine figure this out?

Before Transformers

RNNs processed words one after another:

Prometheus → collects → metrics → It → stores → them

By the time they reached:

It

they had already forgotten much of the earlier context.

Transformer's Idea

Instead of processing sequentially, let every word look at every other word.

Sentence:

Prometheus collects metrics. It stores them.

When processing:

It

the model asks:

Which previous words are important?

Possible scores:

Word	Importance
Prometheus	0.85
collects	0.05
metrics	0.07
stores	0.02
them	0.01

Therefore:

It strongly attends to Prometheus.

This is called Self-Attention.

Query, Key and Value

Each word creates three vectors:

Query (Q)
Key (K)
Value (V)
Human Analogy

Imagine a library.

Query

Question:

I want books about Kubernetes.

This is your Query.

Key

Every book has labels:

Kubernetes
Docker
Terraform
Python

These are Keys.

Value

The actual content of the books.

These are Values.

The process:

Query
 ↓
Compare against Keys
 ↓
Find relevant books
 ↓
Retrieve Values

That's attention.

